{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to run a Python web application inside /srv/web-chroot as the unprivileged appsvc account. It starts automatically through systemd, listens on TCP/8080, survives reboot, and returns HTTP 200. AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created appsvc as a system account with /sbin/nologin.","Built a minimal chroot using the installed Python 3.9 runtime.","Created and enabled chroot-web.service.","Persistently opened TCP/8080 in firewalld.","Verified the process user, chroot root, listener, HTTP content, and boot-time startup.","Safely restarted node1 and verified its boot identity changed and the application fully recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Application runs inside a chroot as unprivileged appsvc.","command_ids":["cmd-e7884c1f7f234062","cmd-c0567b8363834153"],"summary":"The Python process runs as appsvc:appsvc and /proc/<pid>/root resolves to /srv/web-chroot before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Application serves on port 8080.","command_ids":["cmd-fcdb8c811edf4697","cmd-c0567b8363834153"],"summary":"TCP/8080 is persistently allowed, the service listens on 0.0.0.0:8080, and HTTP requests to the managed node address return 200 with the expected page."},{"requirement":"Application starts at boot without an interactive login.","command_ids":["cmd-3a611e8e7d224e1e","cmd-c0567b8363834153"],"summary":"appsvc uses /sbin/nologin; chroot-web.service is enabled and became active automatically after node restart."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed OS release and kernel and use compatible software.","command_ids":["cmd-d4afaf3096e9410b","cmd-fa294e2fa446424b","cmd-c0567b8363834153"],"summary":"AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 remained unchanged; the application uses the platform-installed Python 3.9.21 runtime."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart sequence and recovery.","command_ids":["cmd-3a611e8e7d224e1e","cmd-02da4708344c48ab","cmd-0fa888d401994992","cmd-c0567b8363834153"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID dfdea52d-a1af-4d7b-803a-15f40ee9dd4e was captured, the native reboot was acknowledged, the new boot ID 3444b823-9533-4c6c-b13e-a11d2f31b3d4 proved restart, and service identity, chroot, listener, firewall, data, and HTTP health recovered."}]}
